// Copyright (c) 2026 Roshan. All rights reserved.// Proprietary license — see LICENSE file for details.package com.roshan.persona.security.authimport androidx.room.ColumnInfoimport androidx.room.Entityimport androidx.room.PrimaryKey/** * NOUS — PIN hash entity (Module 12, Pillar 3 — persisted PIN row). * * Strategy §12.3 — the Argon2id hash of the user's app-lock PIN, persisted * to a SQLCipher-encrypted Room table so it survives process death. * * ## Schema * * Single-row table (`id = 0` enforces a singleton PIN; we never store * multiple PINs). Columns: * *   - `hash` — the Argon2id-encoded hash string (contains the salt + params *     inside, per the `de.mkammerer:argon2-jvm` encoding). *   - `salt` — explicit salt column (kept for callers that want to inspect *     the salt without parsing the Argon2 string; also written into the hash). *   - `failed_attempts` — current failed-attempt counter (mirror of *     [com.roshan.persona.security.aidefense.AiAttackDefense] state — useful *     for restoring the lockout window across reboots). *   - `locked_until_ms` — epoch millis when the current lockout expires *     (0 = not locked out). * * ## Threat model * * The hash is stored inside a SQLCipher-encrypted Room database whose * passphrase is wrapped by AndroidKeystore (see [SecurityDatabase]). So an * attacker with physical access to the device file system still faces: * *   1. SQLCipher AES-256-CBC file encryption (key wrapped by Keystore). *   2. Argon2id memory-hard KDF (64 MB per attempt) protecting the PIN. * * Even with the SQLCipher passphrase compromised, brute-forcing a 6-digit * PIN at 64 MB memory per attempt is economically infeasible on commodity * hardware (each attempt costs ~$0.001 in cloud RAM). * * @see PinHashDao * @see SqlCipherPinStorage */@Entity(tableName = "pin_hash")data class PinHashEntity(    @PrimaryKey    val id: Int = PIN_ROW_ID,    @ColumnInfo(name = "hash")    val hash: String,    @ColumnInfo(name = "salt")    val salt: String,    @ColumnInfo(name = "failed_attempts")    val failedAttempts: Int = 0,    @ColumnInfo(name = "locked_until_ms")    val lockedUntilMs: Long = 0L,) {    private companion object {        /** Singleton row ID — only one PIN is ever stored at a time. */        const val PIN_ROW_ID = 0    }}